<title>FRANCE: FRENCH ELECTION - Latest projections at 1800 GMT.</title>
<headline>FRENCH ELECTION - Latest projections at 1800 GMT.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-05-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Following are the latest projections by polling institutes after the first round of France's election for the 577-seat National Assembly, held on Sunday.</p>
<p>The first table gives projections for the share of the popular vote in percentages.</p>
<p>The second table gives projections for the number of seats each party or coalition is likely to win after the June 1 runoff.</p>
<p>The projections are based on actual votes counted in sample constituencies.</p>
<p>-------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p> PROJECTED VOTE		 BVA	  SOFRES	  CSA</p>
<p>-------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p> Communists		     9.6	    9.5	   9.8</p>
<p> Socialists+allies	   29.0	   27.0	  27.3</p>
<p> Ecologists			-	     5.9	   6.5</p>
<p> RPR-UDF+allies		37.2	   31.5	  36.7</p>
<p> National Front		14.8	   15.3	  14.9</p>
<p>-------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>PROJECTED SEATS</p>
<p>-------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p> Extreme left		     0		0	     -</p>
<p> Communists		   15-20	  21-30	     -</p>
<p> Socialists+allies	250-270	242-272	     -</p>
<p> RPR-UDF+allies	   255-275	255-287	     -</p>
<p> National Front		 0-2	    0-3	     -</p>
<p>-------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>BVA polls broadcast by France 2 television and Europe 1 radio SOFRES polls broadcast by TF1 television and RTL radio CSA polls broadcast by France 3 television and Radio France</p>
